/T (In modern web development, it is common for the frontend \(e.g., a JavaScript application running on one port or domain\) to communicate with a backend API hosted elsewhere. Without proper CORS configuration, browsers will block these cross-origin requests. Flask-CORS resolves )
/E (In modern web development, it is common for the frontend \(e.g., a JavaScript application running on one port or domain\) to communicate with a backend API hosted elsewhere. Without proper CORS configuration, browsers will block these cross-origin requests. Flask-CORS resolves )
