/Title (Flask-CORS is an extension for Flask that enables Cross-Origin Resource Sharing \(CORS\) in web applications. CORS is a security feature implemented by web browsers that restricts web pages from making requests to a different domain than the one that served the original content. While this policy helps prevent malicious activities, it can also block legitimate interactions between a frontend application and a backend API hosted on different origins. Flask-CORS simplifies the process of configuring and enabling CORS in Flask applications.)
