/Title (The socket module in Python is a built-in library that enables low-level network communication using standard protocols such as TCP \(Transmission Control Protocol\) and UDP \(User Datagram Protocol\). It provides the foundation for creating client-server applications, allowing systems to communicate over a network using IP addresses and ports.  At its core, a socket represents an endpoint for communication. In a typical client-server model, a server creates a socket, binds it to a specific IP address and port, and listens for incoming connections. A client then creates its own socket and connects to the server. Once the connection is established, both sides can send and receive data.)
