/Title (HTML works closely with other web technologies such as CSS \(Cascading Style Sheets\) and JavaScript. While HTML provides the structure of a webpage, CSS is used to style and format it \(colors, layouts, fonts\), and JavaScript adds interactivity \(dynamic updates, user input handling\). Together, these technologies form the foundation of modern web development.  One of the key features of HTML is its simplicity and readability. It is easy to learn and widely supported across all browsers and platforms. HTML5, the latest version, introduced many new elements and APIs, including support for multimedia \(<audio>, <video>\), semantic elements \(<header>, <footer>, <article>\), and improved form controls. These enhancements allow developers to build more accessible, efficient, and feature-rich web applications.  In the context of your honeypot project, HTML is used to create the frontend dashboard interface. It defines the layout of the dashboard, including tables for displaying attack logs, sections for statistics, and containers for dynamic data updates. Combined with CSS \(e.g., Tailwind CSS\) and JavaScript, HTML enables a responsive and user-friendly interface for monitoring real-time threat activity.)
